<!-- cm_07_ev_v1.xml
     Current Measures v1: Pakistan EV/NEV policy implementation.

     Based on Pakistan's New Energy Vehicle (NEV) Policy 2025-2030:
       2W/3W: 2.05M vehicles by 2030, 50% of new sales by 2030
       4W:    99K vehicles by 2030, 30% of new sales by 2030
       Buses: 2,238 by 2030, 50% of new sales by 2030
       Trucks: 2,996 by 2030, 30% of new sales by 2030
       Ultimate target: 90% of all new vehicle sales by 2040

     v0 had modest SW (0.5→3.0) → produced only 198 PJ transport elec by 2050.
     v1 is much more aggressive to reflect the policy targets:
       - 2W/3W: SW 2.0→8.0 (50% adoption by 2030, 90% by 2040)
       - 4W:    SW 1.0→7.0 (30% adoption by 2030, 90% by 2040)
       - Bus:   SW 1.0→7.0 (50% adoption by 2030, 90% by 2040)
       - Freight: SW 0.5→5.0 (30% adoption by 2030, 90% by 2040)

     NOTE: GCAM share-weights are not penetration percentages. Higher values
     make BEV more competitive in the logit competition. These values are
     calibrated to approximate the policy penetration targets.

     SCOPE: GCAM "Final Energy|Transportation|LDV|Electricity" includes 2W/3W.
     Applied to: trn_pass_road_LDV_4W (Car, Large Car, Mini Car),
                 trn_pass_road_LDV (2W and 3W),
                 trn_pass_road (Bus),
                 trn_freight_road (Light truck)

     RISK: Medium. If model fails, reduce freight/bus SW first, then 4W.
-->
